menu "AMY Synthesizer"

config AMY_USE_FIXEDPOINT
    bool "Use fixed-point arithmetic (s8.23 / s.31)"
    default y
    help
        When enabled (default), AMY uses integer fixed-point arithmetic
        (SAMPLE = s8.23, PHASOR = s.31) instead of single-precision float.

        The ESP32-S3 Xtensa LX7 has a hardware FPU. In practice, float and
        fixed-point perform similarly for most voice counts, but float mode
        may be worth testing. Note: float mode replaces the integer shifts
        inside log2_lut/exp2_lut with ldexpf() calls; ensure you verify
        CPU headroom after switching.

choice AMY_PROFILE_MODE
    prompt "AMY DSP profiling"
    default AMY_PROFILE_OFF
    help
        Instruments the AMY render path with esp_timer timestamps so the
        per-stage CPU cost can be read on-target. Used to measure the
        parallelizable fraction (osc render vs. serial FX/fill_buffer)
        before deciding whether dual-core rendering is worthwhile.

config AMY_PROFILE_OFF
    bool "Off (no profiling, zero overhead)"
    help
        Production default. AMY_PROFILE_START/STOP compile to nothing.

config AMY_PROFILE_COARSE
    bool "Coarse (block-level: render / fill_buffer / deltas)"
    help
        Times only the outer render stages (AMY_RENDER, AMY_FILL_BUFFER,
        AMY_EXECUTE_DELTAS, AMY_ESP_FILL_BUFFER). The per-osc/inner tags
        compile to nothing, so the AMY_RENDER total is NOT inflated by the
        profiler's own timestamp calls. This is the mode to use for the
        Amdahl (parallelizable-fraction) measurement: overhead is ~8
        esp_timer reads per block (<0.1% of the block budget).

config AMY_PROFILE_FULL
    bool "Full (per-osc breakdown, defines AMY_DEBUG)"
    help
        Enables every AMY profiler tag, including per-osc tags that fire
        dozens of times per block INSIDE the AMY_RENDER window. Useful to
        see WHERE render time goes (osc wave vs. filter vs. mix), but the
        per-osc timestamp calls inflate the AMY_RENDER total and overstate
        the parallelizable fraction. Do not use its ratio as the go/no-go
        number; use COARSE for that.

endchoice

config AMY_PROFILE_INTERVAL_MS
    int "Profiler dump interval (ms)"
    depends on !AMY_PROFILE_OFF
    default 5000
    range 500 60000
    help
        How often the accumulated profile is printed to the console and
        reset. Each dump reports per-stage us/block and % of wall time over
        the elapsed window.

endmenu
